⟦ hello.vx — Hello World in VORTHEX
  The simplest possible VORTHEX program.

  Whitespace axes at play:
    - This file uses 0-space indentation → global lattice scope
    - All tokens start in columns 1-40 → Ω stack is the target
    - No blank lines between statements → sequential execution (no RTQ)

  Entropy: every ⟦ ... ⟧ comment is hashed (FNV-1a 32-bit) and XOR'd
  into the entropy register ε.  These comments change program behavior
  if the entropy register affects any operator used here.
  The ⊞ operator is column-independent, so ε has no effect in this file.
⟧

⟦ Define a function that prints "Hello, World!" with a newline.
  Type signature [ → | → ] means: consumes nothing, produces nothing.
  The body pushes a string literal to Ω, then ⊞ pops and prints it. ⟧
⦿ hello [ → | → ]
  «Hello, World!\n» ⊞
⌸0x9B6900C4
⦾

⟦ Top-level execution: call hello ⟧
hello
